      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 10, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4325\", \"desc\": \"For each academic term that is not cancelled, has at least one IAP subject activity with a non-null maximum enrollment, and where the term status is 'Previous', provide the term description, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the maximum enrollment values for IAP subject activities in that term, the academic year description, the term code, term start date, calendar date, day of week, the average calendar year within each calendar year group ordered by term start date, the academic year, and the last day of final exam, ordered by the range of maximum enrollment in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4640\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the term '2017JA', what is the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code, the coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with at least one enrolled student), and the department's school code? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2737\", \"desc\": \"For each person role, provide the person role name, the average, range, and variance of the maximum enrollment values for the activities they lead (considering only activities that are not cancelled and have a specified maximum enrollment), and indicate whether the average maximum enrollment for that role is 'HIGH_CAPACITY' (at least 20% greater than the overall average), 'LOW_CAPACITY' (at least 20% less than the overall average), or 'AVERAGE'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_41\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3131\", \"desc\": \"For each fiscal period, what is the fiscal period description, the variance of the calendar year for all days in that period where the academic year is not null, and whether the variance is 'HIGH_VARIANCE' (at least 20% greater than the average variance across all periods), 'LOW_VARIANCE' (at least 20% less than the average), or 'AVERAGE'? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
