he ASCII values of the course numbers for that subject code\") matches the **dw_4812** DeptSubjectStats pattern: `SIS_DEPARTMENT d JOIN SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = s.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, yielding DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUBJECT_CODE, SUBJECT_CODE_DESC; dw_4812 joins library COURSE_NUMBER to `SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER` and matches DEPARTMENT_NAME = OFFER_DEPT_NAME. The ASCII pattern follows dw_3969 (`AVG(ASCII(...))`); variance follows the VARIANCE() usage in dw_3356/dw_2224.\n\n3. **Differences**: SUBJECT_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY use SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER/DEPARTMENT_NAME and lack COURSE_NUMBER; only LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED carries COURSE_NUMBER + NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS + OFFER_DEPT_NAME, which the question's wording (\"course number\", \"number of enrolled students\") and precedent dw_4584 anchor to. column_concept_enrollment_measures' decision guide confirms NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS for \"number of enrolled students\".\n\n4. Since the DB is unreachable (Access denied on every attempt), the SQL below replicates the verified precedent SQL structures exactly.\n\nFinal query:\n\n",
